Description: LEDS button in the settings menu shows and toggles the LedFx service
 LedFx runs on the Pi as the "ledfx" systemd service (pi/ledfx-*), driving the
 room's WLED strips from Mixxx's Booth output via an ALSA loopback. There is
 no keyboard or shell on the deck, so the settings menu gets a LEDS button
 that shows whether the room lights are live and turns them on and off.
 .
 [Library],ledfx_status (read-only) is 1 while the service is active AND
 NetworkManager reports full or limited connectivity (WLED only needs the
 LAN, not the internet), 0 otherwise; the skin paints the button green or
 red from it. The check is an async /bin/sh run of systemctl + nmcli, on a
 3 s timer that only spawns it while [Skin],show_settings is 1, plus once
 straight away when the cog opens the panel (menu_disarm). A mix in progress
 with the menu closed pays nothing.
 .
 [Library],ledfx_toggle stops the service when the button is green and
 starts it otherwise, through "sudo -n systemctl start|stop ledfx" (the
 passwordless rule pi/ledfx-install.sh installs), then re-polls.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no
